318,0.00445377,0.17129599,-0.06051401,-0.01145704,0.00448925,-0.00459029,-0.03897622,0.01592471,0.01562885,0.02043605,0.00300656,0.10500222,-0.00873123,0.05928045,0.06858817,-0.00745568,-0.00210889,-0.02084121,0.00041292,0.04754256,0.02015531,-0.03443883,-0.03383914,0.05366523,0.00543062,0.01978788,-0.00222761,-0.01108979,0.00075047,0.01673093,-0.04487023,-0.00905705,0.00580381,0.05164517,-0.03519044,0.01305646,-0.01784787,-0.02486882,-0.01147351,0.04308454,-0.04964751,-0.02516586,0.09957995,-0.06766509],"last_embed":{"hash":"sqor97","tokens":407}}},"last_read":{"hash":"sqor97","at":1774939670230},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1774939638694,"size":7265,"at":1774939651600,"hash":"sqor97"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,18],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study":[20,42],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#{1}":[21,25],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#📝 Benim Notlarım":[26,28],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[29,31],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[32,34],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[33,34],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[35,37],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42],"#An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)#{1}":[42,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/X84FIEEQ","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/TH6NIJLK?page=1&annotation=BSNINIAB","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/TH6NIJLK?page=1&annotation=Y5UJAKPS","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/TH6NIJLK?page=1&annotation=UIAZK9ZY","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 10","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/TH6NIJLK?page=10&annotation=6EBKCKHP","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 10","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/TH6NIJLK?page=10&annotation=8VNL7NIT","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/TH6NIJLK?page=6&annotation=FGL2U9Q3","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/TH6NIJLK?page=6&annotation=LRFWCHJL","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 11","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/TH6NIJLK?page=11&annotation=F2DCB3MV","line":42}],"metadata":{"Title":"An AI Dietitian for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus Management Based on Large Language and Image Recognition Models: Preclinical Concept Validation Study","Authors":"Haonan Sun, Kai Zhang, Wei Lan, Qiufeng Gu, Guangxiang Jiang, Xue Yang, Wanli Qin, Dongran Han","Year":2023,"DOI":"10.2196/51300","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"Nutritional management for patients with diabetes in China is a significant challenge due to the low supply of registered clinical dietitians. To address this, an artificial intelligence (AI)–based nutritionist program that uses advanced language and image recognition models was created. This program can identify ingredients from images of a patient’s meal and offer nutritional guidance and dietary recommendatioChatGPT and GPT 4.0 were then tested through the Chinese Registered Dietitian Examination to assess their proficiency in providing evidence-based dietary advice. ChatGPT’s responses to common questions about medical nutrition therapy were compared with expert responses by professional dietitians to evaluate its proficiency. The model’s food recommendations were scrutinized for consistency with expert advice. A deep learning–based image recognition model was developed for food identification at the ingredient level, and its performance was compared with existing models","Findings":"Both ChatGPT and GPT 4.0 passed the Chinese Registered Dietitian examination. ChatGPT’s food recommendations were mainly in line with best practices, except for certain foods like root vegetables and dry beans. Professional dietitians’reviews of ChatGPT’s responses to common questions were largely positive, with 162 out of 168 providing favorable reviews. The multilabel image recognition model evaluation showed that the Dino V2 model achieved an average F1 score of 0.825, indicating high accuracy in recognizing ingredients.ChatGPT has an accuracy rate of 60.5% (121/200) and GPT 4.0 has an accuracy rate of 74.5% (149/200; Table 1). Among the four categories, their accuracy rates are shown in Table 1, with the Food and Nutrition section having the lowest relative accuracy rate and the Public Nutrition and Nutrition Education section having the highest.Most of the errors come from information inaccuracies. The error rates for ChatGPT and GPT 4.0 are 64.6% and 70.6%, respectively.ur results show strong evidence that the LLM-based AI nutritionist program can perform tasks comparable to a registered dietitian in both examination and clinical settings.Our study reveals a significant demand for more immediate and comprehensive nutritional management and education among patients between 20 and 60 years of age predominantly diagnosed with prediabetes or diabetes within the last 5 years","Conclusions":"","Limitations":"Although we have shown that advanced LLM like ChatGPT demonstrated promising results in the registered dietitian exam, responding to frequently asked questions and providing food recommendations, it is essential to note that the model was exposed to only some possible questions a patient might ask.  In addition, it can generate different answers to the same question.","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"sqor97","at":1774939670050}},"smart_blocks:sunAIDietitianType2023a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.03836279,0.02690467,-0.0058013,-0.01166607,0.01225983,0.03091652,-0.00114202,0.04146668,-0.02541914,-0.02181176,0.03109033,-0.1236511,-0.01764499,0.07197485,0.0319248,-0.02000716,0.05293299,-0.02338976,0.02870471,0.00529037,0.05693489,-0.04998469,0.00604822,0.00211346,0.02397284,0.02486114,-0.01189392,-0.01768666,-0.05834185,-0.22420624,0.02145939,0.01633147,0.04902743,-0.02195134,-0.03720469,0.00601812,-0.03832304,0.00606041,-0.08781195,-0.00888258,0.0601514,0.00040118,0.04129142,-0.02778856,0.02676848,-0.0516661,-0.03732623,-0.0306064,-0.06564004,-0.00089417,0.00881663,-0.02018124,0.0419301,0.05022451,0.01387909,0.0228062,0.05901656,0.05353603,0.04679862,0.05714503,0.0289822,0.10890421,-0.20078065,0.07447513,0.01022793,0.06102572,-0.06099427,-0.01529067,0.01237616,-0.04150095,-0.01686056,0.00706